   "text": "Extended Tier Only"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Nuclear fission"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Energy is released from nuclear fuel in nuclear reactors\n- This process of releasing energy is called **nuclear fission**\n\n  - In nuclear** fission**, large nuclei are **split **into smaller nuclei"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Nuclear fission"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2021/05/23.1-Nuclear-fission.png",
   "file": "assets/bbbe4f0d5784-23-1-nuclear-fission.png",
   "alt": "Nuclear fission",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***In nuclear fission, larger nuclei are split into smaller nuclei, releasing lots of energy in the process***"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "** **"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Nuclear fusion"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The Sun releases energy by the process of nuclear **fusion**\n- Nuclear fusion requires extremely high temperature and pressures that can only be found in the core of a star\n\n  - In nuclear **fusion**, small nuclei are **joined **to form larger nuclei"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Nuclear fusion"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/02/nuclear-fusion.png",
   "file": "assets/82526ac35b9a-nuclear-fusion.png",
   "alt": "nuclear fusion, IGCSE & GCSE Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***In nuclear fusion, smaller nuclei are joined into larger nuclei, releasing huge amounts of energy in the process***"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "You are not required to know the details of how nuclear fission and nuclear fusion occur for your exam, but you do need to understand the differences between them."
  }
 ]
